        "name": "USN-8997-2",
        "description": "USN-8997-1 fixed a vulnerability in Net-SNMP. This update provides the corresponding fix for Net-SNMP on Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, Ubuntu 16.04 LTS and Ubuntu 14.04 LTS.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that Net-SNMP incorrectly handled newly accepted  connections in the SMUX module. An unauthenticated remote attacker could  possibly use this issue to cause Net-SNMP to block indefinitely,  resulting in a denial of service.",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2026-89147"
        ]
      },
